rows.en:
What are you agonizing over?
Ahahahaha... you're so weird.
So anyway, we snuck over to those stairs, careful not to get caught by any teachers.{p}

And that was really, really scary.
If it had been at night, I'd definitely have burst into tears.
So we wouldn't miscount, we counted out loud together, all at once.{p}

One... two... three...
Kind of like Okiku, huh?
From Bancho Sarayashiki, you know.{p}

So we decided to leave the old school building.
I was kind of worried about Yoko.
She seemed to be dragging her foot, too, maybe because she twisted it when she fell down the stairs.{p}

So we went down the stairs.
Not thinking about anything in particular.
And then...{p}

"...Thirteen steps."
Yoko muttered it under her breath.
I froze and couldn't help staring at her.{p}

Yoko stopped at the bottom of the stairs, turned around, and looked up.
And she was following the stairs with her eyes.
And then she tilted her head, puzzled, all by herself.{p}

"...That's weird.
There were only thirteen steps."
And then, all of a sudden, she ran back up the stairs.{p}

The hallway was full of tiny babies, crawling around.
I'd never seen anything that scary in my life.
The hallway wasn't even that long, but it felt so, so long.{p}

I remember.
Next time, I'll ask Yoko to let you have one of her babies.
And then I'll sneak it into your room for you, {c}{f:|}.{p}

It's a ring that bleeds, you know?
Nobody would want to get mixed up with that, right?
And so time went by.{p}

She'd been thinking she couldn't stay gloomy and depressed forever, too...
So Ishikawa decided to try taking the ring off.
That ruby ring held too many memories.{p}

And then... it wouldn't come off.
The ring wouldn't budge from her finger.
And from the ruby ring, tears of blood again...{p}

Of course she wasn't going to give up, right?
After that, she went to Mr. Miyama every day and kept begging him to give the ring back.
But Mr. Miyama wouldn't listen at all.{p}

The ruby ring was sitting on the balcony!
There was no doubt it was the one Ogura had given her.
Because both their initials were engraved on the inside of the band.{p}

Yoko and I were both dumbfounded.
With this kind of thing, the mood is everything, isn't it?
We'd worked so hard to build up our fear and curiosity, and she blew it all away in one go.{p}

Sanae didn't care about any of that and kept on climbing.
"...Eleven, twelve, thirteen, fourteen. Huh? There are fourteen steps."
That's what she said...{p}

Yoko was a little bit miffed.
"No fair, Sanae, going on ahead all by yourself!"
"Then I'll wait, so hurry up and come on up."{p}

One step... two steps... three steps...
It's actually pretty nerve-racking, you know.
But then,{p}
